{"hash":"21cc52bb6a788186","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":79.396,"said":"Here in the lane, among the flower stalls, listen to the story the Shiva Purana tells. Long ago, in this southern land, near a mountain called Deva, lived a learned Brahmin named Sudharma, with his wife Sudeha. They loved each other, but they had no child, and the years went by. Sudeha grieved, and at last she begged her husband to marry her younger sister, Ghushma, so that the house would have a son. Sudharma agreed. Ghushma was gentle and devout. Every day she made one hundred and one small lingas from earth, worshipped each one, and then carried them to a lake nearby and let them go into the water. Year after year she did this, and in time she bore a son. The boy was loved by all. He grew up, and he was married. But as Ghushma’s joy grew, something grew in Sudeha’s heart too: jealousy. The Purana says it burned in her like fire, and she told herself that only her sister’s tears could put it out. Walk on with me, down the path to the water. What happened there is the heart of this place.\n\nDid you know? The Shiva Purana says Ghushma went on until she had worshipped a hundred thousand earthen lingas.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1004},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1020,"end":1117}],"words":[[0.098,0.409,0,4],[0.519,0.108,5,7],[0.639,0.084,8,11],[0.735,0.397,12,16],[1.384,0.325,18,23],[1.721,0.072,24,27],[1.805,0.349,28,34],[2.165,0.529,35,41],[2.923,0.373,43,49],[3.307,0.096,50,52],[3.415,0.096,53,56],[3.524,0.445,57,62],[3.98,0.108,63,66],[4.101,0.373,67,72],[4.485,0.457,73,79],[4.954,0.481,80,85],[6.346,0.385,87,91],[6.743,0.385,92,95],[7.332,0.144,97,99],[7.488,0.168,100,104],[7.668,0.312,105,113],[7.993,0.409,114,118],[8.666,0.24,120,124],[8.918,0.048,125,126],[8.978,0.553,127,135],[9.543,0.276,136,142],[9.832,0.457,143,147],[10.469,0.264,149,154],[10.745,0.06,155,156],[10.817,0.337,157,164],[11.166,0.409,165,172],[11.587,0.252,173,178],[11.851,0.625